CLAUDE.md

# Local Claude Code config (per-machine tooling, not GAM software)
.claude/

# Compiled vite configs (artifacts of tsc; source of truth is vite.config.ts)
apps/*/vite.config.js
apps/*/vite.config.d.ts
.vercel

# DB checkpoint dumps are local reset assets — never in git (real data)
deploy/*.dump

# 10/29 (Ben): tesseract.js writes its 5MB language model into the process's
# working directory on first use (cachePath defaults to '.'), which put an
# untracked eng.traineddata at the repo root. The model we actually use is
# committed on purpose at apps/api/assets/tessdata and named by langPath, with
# cacheMethod 'none' so nothing is fetched or written at runtime. This line is
# the belt: a stray copy at the root is never committed by accident.
/*.traineddata
/*.traineddata.gz
# 11/5: and the aside-copy the 10/29 fix left at the root. It was byte-identical
# to apps/api/assets/tessdata/eng.traineddata and would have put 5MB of
# duplicate binary in the repo.
/*.traineddata.moved
